## Short answer
In Express 5 you need no wrapper: when an async route handler throws or its promise rejects, Express calls `next(err)` for you. So the `throw` in `findOrder` (src/app.js:8), awaited in `GET /orders/:id` (src/app.js:13), already reaches Express's error handling. Add one error-handling middleware after your routes, before `app.listen` (src/app.js:18), to answer it your way instead of Express's default 500 page:

```js
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  const status = err.message.startsWith('bad order id') ? 400 : 500;
  res.status(status).json({ error: err.message });
});
```

